commit fb23ed2f8bb1748b89815f870e6ac25bc8d92822
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 09:47:34 2026 +1100

    Prefer the threading oslo.service backend
    
    Unless something picks a backend before oslo.messaging is imported, as
    placement.deploy does, oslo.service uses eventlet. Register threading as
    the default, as glance does; an explicit init_backend() still wins.
    oslo.service[threading] is now a requirement (4.2.0).
    
    This saves nothing alone: it needs futurist's "Do not import eventlet
    until it is needed", and the oslo.utils eventletutils and oslo.messaging
    _utils lazy eventlet changes. With all four, placement uses 63MB of
    anonymous memory, not 73MB.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for import-memory fixes that can be landed one at a
    time and measured in devstack CI; placement and keystone are the
    threaded services that still fall back to the eventlet backend.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (medium effort)
    
    Change-Id: I6629fd997a42108367b09ab37e3a8b7604ad60ba
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

